        "content_text": "<a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/30/well/move/running-loss-grief.html?unlocked_article_code=1.y1A.5ek7.uznoappjJoUr&smid=url-share\">For the roughly 50 million Americans who run regularly, it is rarely just exercise. It is therapy, meditation, community and identity, often all at once. When the body finally says no, the loss can be staggering</a>. (NYTimes gift link, <a href=\"https://archive.is/PGlKA\">archive</a>)",
